When I say beginning, I mean everything up to (and including) Sokoban; I 
generally do the mines after Soko because by that point my character is 
pretty hefty and has plenty of food and possibly a BoH. To me, from the 
mines to around the castle (including the quest and possibly Ludios) is 
the mid-game. Anything after the castle is the end-game; I dislike 
Gehennom very much.

Most of my characters die some silly way before (or in, I've starved to 
death there WITH food) Sokoban; traps, overconfidence on my part, or me 
doing something stupid that I know is stupid but maybe THIS time... it'll 
work. So I see the beginning a lot. Especially Soko, as I do it before 
the mines. 

Of my characters to get to the castle, only two died. One to Air 
Elementals (was totally unprepared for those), and one to a freaking 
Kraken. (Of course, less than 10 of my characters have made it to the 
castle.)

I could do conducts, I suppose, but I don't have the patience for it 
(same for pudding farming). I like hosing Liches with blessed geno, I 
like wishing for G- or SDSM, and I don't have the patience to kill 
everything until it stays dead.

